{"id":1011,"date":"2026-03-18T12:46:45","date_gmt":"2026-03-18T12:46:45","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:10005\/?p=1011"},"modified":"2026-08-30T10:50:40","modified_gmt":"2026-03-23T09:44:07","slug":"%e5%8f%af%e7%a7%bb%e5%8a%a8%e5%a4%a9%e7%ba%bf%e8%b5%8b%e8%83%bd%e7%9a%84%e5%8f%8c%e5%b0%ba%e5%ba%a6%e6%b3%a2%e6%9d%9f%ef%bc%9a%e9%9d%a2%e5%90%91%e5%bc%b9%e6%80%a7%e9%80%9a%e4%bf%a1%e3%80%81%e6%84%9f","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/en\/%e5%8f%af%e7%a7%bb%e5%8a%a8%e5%a4%a9%e7%ba%bf%e8%b5%8b%e8%83%bd%e7%9a%84%e5%8f%8c%e5%b0%ba%e5%ba%a6%e6%b3%a2%e6%9d%9f%ef%bc%9a%e9%9d%a2%e5%90%91%e5%bc%b9%e6%80%a7%e9%80%9a%e4%bf%a1%e3%80%81%e6%84%9f\/","title":{"rendered":"Movable Antenna-Enabled Dual-Scale Beams: Toward Resilient Communications, Sensing, and Security"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-3749991f wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"min-height:1000px\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-vertical is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-458a08b5 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\"><h2 class=\"lab-paper-title wp-block-post-title\">Movable Antenna-Enabled Dual-Scale Beams: Toward Resilient Communications, Sensing, and Security<\/h2>\n\n\n<p class=\"lab-paper-meta has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">SUN C, LI G, WANG S, et al<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"lab-paper-meta has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>IEEE Wireless Communications<\/em><\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-text-color has-contrast-3-color has-alpha-channel-opacity has-contrast-3-background-color has-background is-style-wide\" style=\"margin-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);margin-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20)\"\/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-46005010 lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udccc Abstract<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-pullquote has-text-align-left lab-abstract-quote has-small-font-size\" style=\"margin-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--10);margin-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--10);padding-top:0;padding-right:0;padding-bottom:0;padding-left:0\"><blockquote><p>Future sixth-generation (6G) wireless networks are expected to provide ultra-high data rates, precise sensing capabilities, and robust security guarantees. Movable antenna (MA) technology, by dynamically reconfiguring antenna positions in real time, fully exploits spatial degrees of freedom (DoF) and is poised to become a powerful enabler for an integrated communication-sensing-security framework. The core concept of this article is MA-enabled dual-scale beams\u2014a novel framework that synergistically combines wide beams and narrow beams to achieve adaptive capability across diverse scenarios. This article first introduces the fundamental principles and application scenarios of MA-enabled dual-scale beams, then explores resilient communication strategies and dual-scale beam design to enhance communication robustness; by fusing wide and narrow beams, a two-stage sensing strategy is proposed to improve sensing agility and accuracy; through wide-beam isolation and narrow-beam encryption, dual-scale beams can strengthen physical layer security for massive users. Finally, this article discusses future research directions for advancing the implementation of dual-scale beam technology.<\/p><\/blockquote><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-6adec98e lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udca1 Core Contributions<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<ul start=\"1\" style=\"border-style:none;border-width:0px\" class=\"wp-block-list lab-feature-list\">\n<li class=\"lab-feature-list\"><strong>Proposes a new MA-enabled dual-scale beam framework that uniformly covers communication, sensing, and security scenarios<\/strong>: Seamlessly integrates wide beams (providing broad coverage and graceful degradation in high-mobility scenarios) with narrow beams (providing high gain and rapid recovery in precise-CSI scenarios). By dynamically adjusting MA positions and precoding, the system can adaptively switch under varying channel conditions, overcoming the fundamental limitations of fixed antenna arrays in beamwidth adjustment.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li class=\"lab-feature-list\"><strong>Designs dual-scale communication beams to achieve resilient communication<\/strong>: To address the issue of narrow-beam failure caused by outdated CSI in high-mobility scenarios, wide beams combined with robust precoding provide graceful degradation guarantees; when CSI is accurate, MAs reposition to optimal locations and activate narrow beams for rapid performance recovery. Simulation results in Fig. 3 demonstrate that MA-enabled dual-scale beams achieve significantly higher sum rates than single fixed narrow-beam schemes in high-mobility scenarios.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li class=\"lab-feature-list\"><strong>Proposes a two-stage dual-scale sensing strategy, enabling hierarchical sensing from coarse scanning to precise localization<\/strong>: In the first stage, MAs configure wide beams for rapid scanning of large areas and preliminary target localization (minimizing CRB); in the second stage, the system switches to highly directional narrow beams for precise target measurement. The CRB comparison results in Fig. 4 show that MA arrays consistently achieve the lowest CRB among all antenna configurations, yielding optimal sensing accuracy.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li class=\"lab-feature-list\"><strong>Designs dual-scale secure beams, providing layered security guarantees of wide-beam isolation and narrow-beam encryption for massive users<\/strong>: Wide beams isolate user groups into different spatial regions to eliminate cross-region interference, while narrow beams enable directional encrypted transmission or physical layer secret key generation within each isolated region. The key generation rate comparison in Fig. 5 demonstrates that the MA-enabled dual-scale scheme outperforms all other schemes.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-2f9d57f4 lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udd27 Method Overview<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-831b2db5 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-image uagb-block-b46d2053 wp-block-uagb-image--layout-default wp-block-uagb-image--effect-static wp-block-uagb-image--align-none wp-container-content-9cfa9a5a\"><figure class=\"wp-block-uagb-image__figure\"><img decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-40-50.png ,https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-40-50.png 780w, https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-40-50.png 360w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 480px) 150px\" src=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-40-50.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"uag-image-1014\" width=\"849\" height=\"487\" title=\"PixPin_2026-03-18_20-40-50\" loading=\"lazy\" role=\"img\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"lab-experiment-caption has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">The core of an MA system lies in mounting antennas on three-dimensional mechanical rails, where a central processing unit drives stepper motors to reposition antennas to target locations, thereby achieving real-time beamwidth optimization by altering physical path lengths between antennas (rather than merely adjusting phases).<strong>Dual-scale beam design<\/strong>Comprises two core elements: first, channel parameter estimation based on real-time CSI (angle of arrival, delay, path gain) to construct the physical layer MA channel model; second, joint optimization of MA positions and precoding matrices to form the required wide\/narrow beam combinations across communication, sensing, and security tasks. In communication scenarios, wide beams cooperate with robust precoding to guarantee connectivity for mobile users, while narrow beams restore high-speed transmission under low mobility or precise CSI conditions; in sensing scenarios, a two-stage strategy sequentially performs wide-beam environment scanning and narrow-beam precise localization; in security scenarios, wide and narrow beams operate simultaneously, serving user spatial isolation and directional secure transmission, respectively. Deep neural networks (DNNs) can further assist scenario identification and MA position prediction, reducing online optimization latency.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-dda34f26 lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udcca Experimental Results<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-831b2db5 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-image uagb-block-080de2b0 wp-block-uagb-image--layout-default wp-block-uagb-image--effect-static wp-block-uagb-image--align-none wp-container-content-432d1f4f\"><figure class=\"wp-block-uagb-image__figure\"><img decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-41-49.png ,https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-41-49.png 780w, https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-41-49.png 360w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 480px) 150px\" src=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-41-49.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"uag-image-1015\" width=\"400\" height=\"400\" title=\"PixPin_2026-03-18_20-41-49\" loading=\"lazy\" role=\"img\"\/><figcaption class=\"uagb-image-caption\">Fig.4<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-image uagb-block-b357864e wp-block-uagb-image--layout-default wp-block-uagb-image--effect-static wp-block-uagb-image--align-none wp-container-content-432d1f4f\"><figure class=\"wp-block-uagb-image__figure\"><img decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-43-12.png ,https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-43-12.png 780w, https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-43-12.png 360w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 480px) 150px\" src=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-43-12.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"uag-image-1016\" width=\"400\" height=\"400\" title=\"PixPin_2026-03-18_20-43-12\" loading=\"lazy\" role=\"img\"\/><figcaption class=\"uagb-image-caption\">Fig.5<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-831b2db5 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-7cf84ebf wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\" style=\"padding-top:0;padding-bottom:0\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-image uagb-block-840a35ae wp-block-uagb-image--layout-default wp-block-uagb-image--effect-static wp-block-uagb-image--align-none wp-container-content-432d1f4f\"><figure class=\"wp-block-uagb-image__figure\"><img decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-43-26.png ,https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-43-26.png 780w, https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-43-26.png 360w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 480px) 150px\" src=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-43-26.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"uag-image-1017\" width=\"600\" height=\"500\" title=\"PixPin_2026-03-18_20-43-26\" loading=\"lazy\" role=\"img\"\/><figcaption class=\"uagb-image-caption\">Fig.3<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"lab-experiment-caption has-medium-font-size wp-container-content-432d1f4f wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>MA consistently achieves the lowest CRB among all antenna configurations, yielding optimal sensing accuracy; the fixed half-wavelength-spaced array exhibits significantly higher CRB with pronounced performance degradation<\/strong>: As shown in <strong>Fig. 4<\/strong> As shown, the CRB curves of the MA array consistently remain at the lowest level; although the sparse fixed antenna array approaches MA performance, a gap remains, while the standard half-wavelength fixed array exhibits significantly higher CRB, validating MA's fundamental advantage in sensing accuracy. Furthermore,<strong>Fig. 3<\/strong> The high-mobility scenario simulations show that the sum rate of MA dual-scale beams outperforms fixed antenna schemes,<strong>Fig. 5<\/strong> The key generation rate comparison also demonstrates that the MA-enabled scheme achieves the best performance in physical layer secret key generation scenarios.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-e3c2d50d lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udcdd Citation<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<pre class=\"wp-block-code lab-bibtex-code has-small-font-size\"><code>@article{sun2026madualscale,\n  author    = {Chen Sun and Guyue Li and Shuai Wang and Guanghui Wen},\n  title     = {Movable Antenna Enabled Dual-Scale Beams for Resilient Communication, Sensing and Security},\n  journal   = {IEEE Wireless Communications},\n  year      = {2026},\n  month     = feb,\n  doi       = {10.1109\/MWC.2025.3622920}\n}\n<\/code><\/pre>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-wide\" style=\"margin-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);margin-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20)\"\/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\">\n<div style=\"height:100px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-content-justification-space-between is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-788841da wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>This paper first introduces the fundamental principles and application scenarios of MA-enabled dual-scale beams, then explores resilient communication strategies and dual-scale beam design to enhance communication robustness; by integrating wide and narrow beams, a two-stage sensing strategy is proposed to improve sensing agility and accuracy; through wide-beam isolation and narrow-beam encryption, dual-scale beams can strengthen physical layer security for massive users. Finally, this paper discusses future research directions to advance the implementation of dual-scale beam technology.<\/p>","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":1014,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"mypost","format":"standard","meta":{"_uag_custom_page_level_css":"","footnotes":""},"categories":[5],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-1011","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-research"],"uagb_featured_image_src":{"full":["https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-40-50.png",849,487,false],"thumbnail":["https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_20-40-50-150x150.png",150,150,true],"medium":["https:\